      "side": 1,
      "message": "I observe below restore behaviour when proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() returns DEAD_OBJECT all the time.\nWithout fix proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() is called for the same mSequence id twice.\nLooks that protection that prevents from unnecessary track recreation (\"// re-create track, unless someone else has already done so\") does not allow to recreate track after proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() returned DEAD_OBJECT error while mSequence id was not changed meanwhile (noone else called restoreTrack_l()).\n\nWithout fix:\nmSequence\u003d2: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d3\nmSequence\u003d3: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nmSequence\u003d3: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d4\nmSequence\u003d4: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nmSequence\u003d4: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d5\nmSequence\u003d5: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nbreak\n\nWith fix:\nmSequence\u003d2: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d3\nmSequence\u003d3: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d4\nmSequence\u003d4: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d5\nmSequence\u003d5: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d6\nmSequence\u003d6: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nrestoreTrack_l() -\u003e mSequence\u003d7\nmSequence\u003d7: proxy-\u003eobtainBuffer() -\u003e DEAD_OBJECT\nbreak",
